.Dd September 20, 2026
.Dt MPUTEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mputest
.Nd check the memory protection map from user mode
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the kernel's report of the Cortex-M0+ memory protection unit through
.Xr sysctl 8
.Pq Va machdep.mpu
and checks it from unprivileged code.
It forks one child per probe address and records whether the child read the
word or died of
.Dv SIGSEGV .
.Pp
Kernel RAM above the process window, kernel text in XIP flash and the SIO
block must be closed when
.Va machdep.mpu.enable
reads 1 and open when it reads 0.
The boot ROM and the top of the process window must be open in both states.
.Va machdep.mpu.nregions
must read the datasheet's eight, and enable must be set only when
.Va machdep.mpu.programmed
equals the three regions the kernel's map holds.
.Pp
Each probe prints one line ending in
.Dq ok
or
.Dq FAIL ;
the last line is
.Dq MPUTEST OK
followed by the MPU state, or
.Dq MPUTEST FAIL
and the count of disagreements.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The number of probes that disagreed with the kernel's report, or 2 when
.Xr sysctl 3
or
.Xr fork 2
failed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh CAVEATS
Each closed probe under an enabled MPU is a real HardFault, and the kernel
prints its fault frame on the console before killing the child, so a run
with the MPU on produces three fault reports between the probe lines.
